# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# The repos are configured with core.autocrlf=input, which normalises only on
# commit and leaves the working tree as whatever tool wrote it. That is how
# source files here ended up with *mixed* endings - e.g. global/routes.ts had
# 351 CRLF lines and LF lines in the same file - which silently breaks
# exact-text patching and makes diffs noisy. Declaring it here makes the rule
# travel with the repo instead of depending on each clone's local config.
#
# NOTE: this governs git only; it does not rewrite files already on disk.
# Run `git add --renormalize .` once at a natural commit point to fix those.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets - never touch these
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.otf  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.bson binary

# Generated lockfiles: keep diffs collapsed in review
package-lock.json -diff
